        <p>Workhouse New Infirmary,—WANTED, ,able r-bodtihede oGuT"ljNi. MAN, to act as Male Attendant or Hospital Porter; also a WOMAN as General Servant in Nurses Home, a married couple under the ages of 40, without encumbrance preferred. Wages, man £2.5. woman £2O. per annum, with rations, uniffirm and apartments subject to the deductions wader the Superannuation Act of 1896. Particulars of the duties may be had upon application to the Master of filo Workhouse. Applications with not more than three recently dated certificates of character and ability to be sent to the Master of the Workhouse not later than THURSDAY, the 6th day Of September next. Reasonoble travelling expenses will be allowed to selected candidates. By order. CHARLES HARRALL WARD, Master of the Warrington Union Workhouse,</p>
        <p>22nd August. 1900. ANTARRINGTON UNION.—PERSONS willing to CONTRACT for the supply of any of the under- mentioned articles from Michaelmas to Lady Day next, except where stated for a year, to be delivered free of expense at the Warrington Union Workhouse, or at the Industrial Schools. Padgate. at such times and in such quantities as the Board of Guardians shall dirket. are requested to send in TENDERS, properly sealed, endorsed, and free of expense, addressed to the Clerk to the Guardians, before four o'clock p.m. on TUESDAY. the 11th day of SEPTEMBER inst. The following are the articles for which TENDERS are required : C:oceries and Provisions Shoes, Clogs and Slippers Beef and Mutton Glazing „ Joints for Officers Brushes S• Milk for a year Coffins Flour and Irish pin head meal Best Oakum rope for picking Loaves and Bread Best Penmaenmawr Stone Beer and Porter for breaking purposes Straw and Potatoes Leather</p>
        <p>Drapery &amp;c. Cord and Twill</p>
        <p>Coal, black, and Gas Coke Samples of any of the above may be seen on application to the Master of the Workhouse. The Coal and Slack supplied must he to the satisfaction of the House and Schools Com- mittees. The Pit and quality of coal must be named in the Tender. Forms of tender and full particulars as to th 9 probable quantities of eal.h article required may be obtained at the Clerk's Office. Each tender must be made upon the prescribed form and pros erly enclosed and endorsed with the name of the ar tide tendered for. Each article tendered for must be of size ma' 7rial and quality shown at the Workhouse. No tenders othsr articles Will be accepted. Hach erintreetor must be I spared (if required) to enter into security for the due erformanCe of his contract. The Guardians do not bind themselves to accept the lowest or any tender. All contract accounts will be paid quarterly _By order. JAMh CLOWES SUTTON, Clerk to the Guardians. Bewley Chambers, Warrington, September Ist, 1900.</p>
