      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-08-31_WidnesExaminer_art0077" n="art0077">
        <head>HEALTH AND STRENGTH.</head>
        <p>HEALTH AND STRENGTH.</p>
        <p>Nature's best gifts are those that contribute towards health and strength. The active prieciple of the best remedial a gents (sarsaparilla,burdock, gentian,lavender, saffron, dandelion, and quinine) constitute Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, the most reliable tonic, purely vegetable.-Alealth has many handmaids, and all depend on i-trength of nerve and muscle. We exact too much from these in t he daily competitive struggle for success in life, and we have to suffer in consequence—indiges- tion, weakness, nervousness, sleeplessness, liver dis- orders, chest affections, and numerous other complaints. Now all these are successfully combatted with the sus- taining assistance of Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, the best remedy of the age. It is safe, sure, and per- manent in its effrct. If you find that your system is unable to bear the oppressive heat, and you are almost unable t I follow your daily vccation, immediately strengthen your constitution by taking a course 'of Gwilym Evan's Quinine Bitters. They make tee weak strong, and give new heart and ago" to the weary toiler. They revive the spirits and etrengthen the nerves. By giving tone to the whole constitutien they ward off fevers and other ailments. No family should be without a bottle. An occasional dose taken when a man has felt slightly out of sorts, has prevented many a long illness. We assert the above Confi- dently. Man is much more subject to the influence of his surroundings than is generally supposed. The ill effects upon the general health of living in close ill- ventilated, and badly-lit homes, offices, or workshops. are, of course, well-known to everyone who has studied hygiene; while the life giving effects of sunlight and fresh air are equally well known. The same may be said of the results of the various climatic changes. The injuri- ous effects of a prevailing east wind are evident to all observant persons ; and the depressing influ-nce of an approaching thunderstorm on some constitutions has also been observed by mespeople. Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters may be termed an insurance policy against" catching cold." for it gives stamina and a healthy vitality to resist climatic changes and is a reliable safeguard against colds, chills, and coughs, which frequently happen through the weakness of the constitution being unable to resist the effects of the changeableness of the weather. Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters never disappoints when given a fair trial, and no medicine has had so many imitators, but the purchaser has the remedy against such deceit in hisown hands. Note particularly the name " Gwilym Evans" on the label, on the stamp, andon the bottle (a threefold precaution),without which none are genuine. Refuse all others then you will have the satisfaction of benefitting by the unrivalled virtues of this groat tonic. Gwilvm Evans' Quinine Bitters is sold in bottles 2s. 9d. and 4s. ed. each by chemists and patent medicine venders, or will be sent direct by the proprietors, without any E xtra charge to any address in the United Kingdom. Sole Proprietors :—Quinine Bitters Manufacturing Company, Limited, Llanelly. South Wales.</p>
