        <p>Cheshire Agricultural Show. The Cheshire Agricultural Show Wets held on Wednesday in beautiful weather in te public park at Congleton. The total number of ,entries was 1,203, of which 308 were horses and 135 cattle. There were 77 exhibits of cheese and butter. There was a very fine show of heavy and light norses,dairy cattle, and sheep, but under the Board of Agricul • ture's rules the exhibition of swine was prohibited. In the light horse section prizes were awarded to Mr Ferguson, of Batley; J Makeague, of Newton- le-Willows; J W M'Fie, Chester; A C Sparkes, of Altrincham. Mr Lees Knowles, was awarded first prize for hackneys in the heavy horse class. The first prize for shire stallions went to Thomas Lowndes, of Tatbury, and for mare or gelding to Lord Egerton. Several firsts in this class were awarded to J W Kenworthy, of Keleall. In the shorthorn cow class Mr Her-Colville, of Bellaport Hall, was awarded two prizes. The first prize for the best dairy caw went to Samuel Gould,of Lymin, and for the pair of dairy cows to Richard Clarke, of Warburton Park. Prizes for long woollyd rams went to Russell Ward, Great Warford, and others to John Ward, Stantherne, and Charles Hollinshead, Sandbach. There was keen competition in the dairy classes, in cheese notably. e FRB&amp; TO RHBUM&amp;TIO ANDePAR&amp;LYTIC</p>
