      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-08-31_WidnesExaminer_art0108" n="art0108">
        <head>VOLUNTEER INTELLIGENCE.</head>
        <p>VOLUNTEER INTELLIGENCE.</p>
        <p>Runcorn.</p>
        <p>On Monday the annual prize meeting of the F and G Companies (Runcorn detachmeat) of the 'and V.B. Cheshire Regiment took place at Owley Wood Range, aear Northwich. There were 53 rank and file present, under the command of Captain Ashton and Sergeant- Instructor Callaghan. There was a grey light, the wind remaining steady from the rear during the whole of the proceedings. Some very good shooting took place. The prize money amounted to about £5O.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-08-31_WidnesExaminer_art0109" n="art0109">
        <head>DETACHMENT COMPETITION.</head>
        <p>DETACHMENT COMPETITION.</p>
        <p>There were thirty prizei offered in this eampeition, ranging fro-n 5s to £3. Seven shots each were fired at 200 yards. 500 yard, and 600 yards. The highest passible score was 105.</p>
        <p>200 500 6;0 To-</p>
