        <p>G</p>
        <p>203 500 To- yds yds Drills W. Uolour-Sergeant W H Harvey 32 ... 35 ... 13k ... 831 Lance-Sergeant J F Edwards 35 ... 31 ... 131 ... 791 Sergeant W Cooper Corporal J Houghton Private W Gregory Corporal C Bradbury Sergeant D Edwards Corporal W Griffiths Private J Hargreaves Lance-Sergeant W F Gaskell 31 ... 18 ... 9 ... 58</p>
        <p>EXTRA SERIES COMPETITION.</p>
        <p>Five shots each kneeling at 200 yards. The prizes are given by the Runcorn tradesmen. Result :-1, Lance- Sergeant F Edwards, 25, points '• 2, Corporal J. Mort, 24.; 3, Sergeant J Rushton, 24; 4, Sergeant D Edwards, 24 ;5. Colour-Sergeant Harvey,24; 6. Private W Gregory. 24 ; 7, Lance-Corporal J Sadler, 23 ; 8, Corporal W Griffiths' 23 ; 9, Colour-Sergeant J Mort. 23 ; 10, Corporal J Houghton, 23; 11, Lance-Srrgeant J Gittins. 23; 12, Seigeant S D Matthews, 22 • 13, Corporal J Marsh, 22; 14, Corporal C Bradbury, 22 ; 15, Lance- Corporal R Jones, 21; 16, Privati T P Mort, 21 ; 17, Sergeant %V Cooper, 21; 18, Private J Hargreaves, 21 ; 19. Private R Shaw, 20 ; 20, Private W Moors, 20; 21. Private W Freeman, 20; 22. Private T Mellor, 20.</p>
        <p>RECRIJIT3 COMPETITION.</p>
        <p>Fourteen Rtotg each at 200 yart-TS, sewn kueeling and seven prone. Eight prizes were given, and a valuable silver challenge cup to tha highest scorer. Result :-1, Private F W Dutton. cup, 57 points; 2, Private W Moors 54 ; 3,Private T Mellor. 54 ; 4. Private H Bill, 51 ; 5, Private Carruthers, 51 ; 6. Private Woodier, 46 ;7, Private H Houghton,46 ; 8, Private A Horrocks, 45.</p>
