        <p>Continuing the good work of augmenting the fund far the Cottage Hospital, Sunday afternroa saw a very 90- cessful open air concert given on Runcorn Hill, by the Volunteer Brass Band and their friends, the collecting at which amounted to £5 12s 21. Again, on Wednesday evening, there was a caPital magic lantern exhibition given at the Drill Hall, Cireery way-road, when through the kindness of the "Lirerpoll Express " proprietors, two of their staff attended, auci exhibited their beautiful collection 01 about 200 w„arj pictures. The auSience was fairly large, some £6 18i being taken at the door. Tee same occasion was uoe's by the Cycle Parade Committee, ;for the distribution 0' their prizes, a task which was fulfilled by Mrs Coogrele. of Moore, in a gracaul and dignified manner. cos 9 Mr. A R Norman C.C., intimated how pleased be - e to take the chair that evening, to help forward 009 Cottage Hospital scheme. He thcught it ought to nsencaoned that the chief praise in connectise with 01 affair was due to the Runcorn Cycle Club. (Applaer,,,.. But whilst acknowledging that as gratefully as t'7o could they should also remember that great praise P7:3 due to those persons who bad also forwardel a prowls', substantial subscriptioo,—(hear, hear),—and to all thaq who were doing their best to help forward the causei,bue the Cottage Hospital in Runcorn. (Hear, bear.) is financial results up to the present were e—AesounS,,o hand prior to the last cycle parade £631 ; profit iue, the sale of confetti £6 is 4d ; big loaf £2 ; publichot' collections £2 8s 5d ; Sunday concert collection t`ci 12s 2d ; street collections £34. 12; 9.1 ; total £5O 14s If; or a grand total of £6Bl 141 BN. (Applause.) pile Norman then called upon Mrs Congreve to distribute prizes. teell Mrs. Congreve, who was most cordial:3s reeeived nest handed the prizes to the following winners: dressed ladies' machine : 1. Miss Watson Charlesworth. Neatest ladies' costume : 1, Miss PS, 2, Miss Watson. Neatest 