        <p>DR. J. COLLIS BROWNE CHLORODYNE. THE ORIGINAL AND ONLY GENUINE. CfILORODYNE is admitted by the Profession to be the most wonderfal and valuable remedy ever dl. covered. QHLORODYNE is tbe best remedy known for Coughs, Consumption. Bronchitis and Asthma. CIILORODYNE effectually checks and arrests those too often fatal diseases—Diphtheria, Fever Oroup Ague. CHLORODYNE acts like a charm in Diarrhcea and is the only specific in Cho!erased Dysentary. CIaLORODYNE effectually cuts short all attacks of Epilepsy. Hysteria. Palpitation, and Spasms. 011LORODYNE is the only palliative in Neural- k./ gia, Rheumatism, Gout, Cancer. Toothache, Meningitis, From Dr. B. J. BOULTON AND CO., Hon:mastle. We have made pretty extensive use of Ohlorodyne inour practice lately and look upon it as an excellent direct Seda- tive and Anti-spasmodic. It seems to allay pain and irrita- tion in whatever organ, and from wbatever cause. It induces a feeling cf comfort and quietude r Jt obtainable by any other remedy, and it seems to posses , this great advantage over all other sedatives; that it eaves no unpleasant after effects. " Earl Russell communicated to the College of Physicians that he received a despatch from het Maj..ty's Oonsul at Manilla to the effect that Cholera had been raging fearfully, and that the ONLY remedy of any service was CHLOE°. DYNE."—See Lancet, Ist December, 1864. IAUIION.—BEWARE, OF PIii,ACY AND IMITA- TIONS. CAUTlON.—Vice•Chdnebllor lir W. PAGE WOOD stated that Dr. J. COLLIS BROWNE was. anloubtedly, the inventor " 0 I-I LORODYNE " and that the story of the defendant FREEMAN, was deliberately untrue. which he regretted to say had been sworn to.—See Times, 13th July, 1864. Sold in bottles at le. 116_ .I's. 9d., and 4s. 6d. None is genuine without the words "DR. J COLLIS BROW:life CHLORODY/SE "on the Government Stamp. Overwhelm- ng Medina testimony accompanies each bottle.</p>
