        <p>BE WISE IN TIME AND FURNISH AT pars's, LONDON-ROAD, MANCHESTER (Just past Station, through Railway Arch) ; OR AT PITTS'S NEW BRANCH, p ITTS'S, PANTHEON, GAYTHORN (Just past Manchester Central Station). Business Hours, 8 to 7; Saturdays 8 to 9. THE OLDEST FIRM IN THE TRADE. THAT HOPE DEFERRED MAKETH THE HEART SICK is just as true now as ever it was will be attested by all Whose most cherished aspirations have remained unfulfilled. In every walk of life we encounter this hankering after the (supposed) unattainable, whilst in many cases the remedy is close at hand if those interested only knew how to avail themselves of it. It affects most businesses, the furnishing trade especially. For instance, a young man rceets a maiden fair whose appearance and merits he approves. She, likewise, appreciates his qualities, and quickly an affection sprtegs up between them. How pleasant they think it would be to marry and start housekeeping together. Then the stumbling block presents itself--where is the cash to purchase furniture to come from ? With him, time past, like with most young fellows, "enough for the day has been the evil thereof." He has saved practically nothing so the marriage is postponed indefinitely. Now, this is where PITTS S step in with a timely suggestion. Instead o! deferring the hope and making the hearts sick why not, by a fair and equitable arrangement, defer the payments and make both hearts glad? FITTS'S offer to supply the requisite house-furnishing articles at lowest cash prices on payment of a trifling deposit and remainder by easy instalments charging 10 per cent only for the convenience. PITTS'S during the last half century, have furnished thousands of homes in this manner that never would have been furnished otherwise. Now act promptly, and call at PITTS'S. of LONDON-ROAD and GAYTHORN. PITTS'S PEERLESS HOUSES OF FURNITURE at 151, 221, 284', 384', 50,75,100, 203, up to 1,900 guineas, are the embodiment of everything that is excellent and necessarylfor the embellishment of the home. They are incomparably superior in VALUE and appearance to others. They comprise articles of rarest beauty though thoroughly substantial, and can be had for ABOUT HALF expensive city prices. Full particulars and ILLUSTRATED FUR- NISHING GUIDE, containing 700 artistic designs prieed, post free. DITTS'S'DINING-ROOM FURNITURE.—Astonnd- A. ing display of Suites in Morocco, Saddlebags. Velvet, and other costly fabrics. For instance, splendid Suite, American walnut, covered with rich Utrecht velvet; cost £45, Pitts's price £l5 lOs Handsome Sideboard, to match cost £25. Pitta's price £lO les. Extending Dining-table, cost £7, for £3 3s. Grand Suite American walnut and I Arabian saddlebags ; cost 50 guineas, Pitt's price £lB. Magnificent Brown Oak Suite, in real morocco leather ; cost 60 guineas, Pitts's price 25 guineas. Colossal Solid Oak Sideboard, to match, profusely carved ; cost £B5, Pitts's price £35. Serviceable Suite, in real leather, £7 10s, cost £2O; another in velvet, 2.8 Bs, cost £22, Sideboard, three bevelled plates in black, £4 5s ; worth double. Scores to select from. Sideboards, Dining-tables, Dinner Waggons, every size, make, and design, in endless profusion at giving- away prices. DITTo'6 DRAWING-ROOM. FURNITUR E.—A 1 superb collection of choicest, designs, mach as Chippen- dale, Sheraton. Adams, Louis, &amp;c., tu , in rosewood, beauti- fully inlaid, Circassian and Italian walnut, &amp;e.. upholstered with every conceivable variety of coverings. including Genoa and frieze velvets, brocatelle, cotclaine. &amp;c. Chippendale Suite, in dark mahogany, cost £53. Pitta's price 24 guineas ; overmantel to match, cost £IO, Pitts's price 6 guineas ; also Cabinet, cost £55, Pitts's price 20 guineas; Italian Walnut Suite, in rich velvet, cost £35, Pitts's price 10 guineas ; one In Tapestry, cost £3O, Pitts's price 12 guineas ; another in embossed velvet. cost £2l, Pitts's price 8 guineas ; Bitting. room Suite, complete. cost 